To automatically tag unlabeled IPv4 prefixes with the link-bandwidth attribute for direct EBGP peerings, use the following configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    group "EBGP_GROUP"
        link-bandwidth
            add-to-received-ebgp ipv4
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Key details:**  
- This configures BGP to add the link-bandwidth extended community to all received unlabeled IPv4 routes from directly connected EBGP peers in the specified group.  
- Replace `EBGP_GROUP` with your actual BGP group name containing the external neighbors.  
- The attribute is applied automatically to routes upon reception, enabling dynamic inbound traffic engineering based on circuit capacity.  

For neighbor-specific application (if required):
```
configure router bgp
    group "EBGP_GROUP"
        neighbor 192.0.2.1
            link-bandwidth
                add-to-received-ebgp ipv4
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```
