To address the issue of unimported VPN-IPv4 and VPN-IPv6 routes not being utilized due to unresolved next-hops, configure the following on your Nokia 7750 SR:

```cli
configure router bgp
    enable-rr-vpn-forwarding
    next-hop-resolution
        use-bgp-routes
    exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `enable-rr-vpn-forwarding` forces all received VPN-IP routes (regardless of route targets) into a dummy VRF for next-hop resolution. This maintains route isolation while allowing BGP next-hops to be resolved using tunnels defined under `next-hop-resolution`.  
- `use-bgp-routes` under `next-hop-resolution` enables recursive resolution of BGP next-hops via other BGP routes (up to 4 levels), ensuring unlabeled IPv4/IPv6 routes can forward traffic properly.  

These commands ensure unresolved VPN routes are processed while preserving VPRN isolation.
