To enforce a one-hour LLGR stale time and override peer-advertised values, configure the following:

```cli
configure router bgp graceful-restart
    long-lived
        advertised-stale-time 3600
        helper-override-stale-time 3600
    exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `advertised-stale-time 3600` sets the local LLGR stale time to one hour (3600 seconds) in BGP updates.  
- `helper-override-stale-time 3600` forces peers to use this local stale-time value instead of their advertised values.  

**Deployment Notes:**  
- Apply this configuration globally under `graceful-restart>long-lived` to ensure consistency across all address families and peers.  
- Verify existing BGP sessions remain stable post-configuration by monitoring session resets (`show router bgp summary`).  
- Use `show router bgp neighbor <ip> capabilities` to confirm the advertised/override values are active.  

**Stability Considerations:**  
- The override setting only affects inbound routes from peers, preventing routing flaps during BGP convergence.  
- Test changes in a maintenance window to validate peer compatibility with the 1-hour stale timer.
