**Key details:**  
- Apply `aggregate-used-paths ipv4` under the BGP group facing Juniper peers (replace `"JUNIPER_PEERS"` with your group name).  
- This command aggregates bandwidth values from link-bandwidth extended communities of used multipaths when re-advertising routes with next-hop-self.  
- It ensures the summed bandwidth of parallel links is preserved during internal redistribution for load balancing.  

No additional commands are required if Juniper peers already include link-bandwidth communities. If communities are missing, first validate EBGP neighbor configurations on Juniper devices to transmit bandwidth metrics.
