"During a multi-vendor network migration, we're encountering scenarios where our Nokia 7750 SR routers need to temporarily advertise suboptimal BGP routes to maintain connectivity while we phase out legacy equipment. What's the proper configuration approach to override the default best-path selection behavior and ensure these alternative routes get propagated to downstream peers?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To temporarily override the default BGP best-path selection and ensure suboptimal routes are advertised during your migration, use the following configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        ignore-router-id
    exit
exit
```

This configuration disables BGP router ID comparison during best-path selection. When new paths equivalent to the current best path (except for router ID) are received, the existing best path is retained—even if the new path has a lower router ID. This ensures stable propagation of your intended routes to downstream peers during the migration.
