To implement BGP dampening on your Nokia 7750 SR routers to mitigate route flaps while minimizing delays for stable paths, use the following CLI configuration:

1. **Define a route policy with tuned damping parameters**:
```cli
/configure router policy-options
begin
route-policy "damping-policy"
    damping half-life 10 reuse 1500 suppress 3000 max-suppress-time 45
exit
commit
```

2. **Apply the damping policy globally under BGP**:
```cli
/configure router bgp
damping route-policy "damping-policy"
exit
```

**Explanation of Parameters**:
- **`half-life 10`**: Penalty decay time reduced to 10 minutes (default 15) to clear stability faster.
- **`reuse 1500`**: Reuse threshold raised to 1500 (default 750) to reinstate routes quicker.
- **`suppress 3000`**: Suppress threshold kept conservative at 3000 to target only unstable prefixes.
- **`max-suppress-time 45`**: Maximum suppression capped at 45 minutes (default 60) to limit penalty duration.

**Verification Commands**:
```cli
show router bgp routes damping
