```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name> local-preference 200
```

Replace `<group-name>` with the BGP group name of your preferred transit provider. This sets a default local preference of 200 for all routes received from peers in this group that do not already include the attribute.

If you need to apply this to a specific neighbor within the group:
```cli
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> local-preference 200
```
Replace `<ip-address>` with the neighbor's IP address. 

