To ensure optimal path diversity and bidirectional multipath capability for IPv4 prefixes in your multicast VPN deployment, configure the BGP add-paths feature for multicast VPN IPv4 routes at the neighbor, group, or global BGP level. Here are the CLI commands:

**1. Neighbor-level configuration (recommended for granular control):**
```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <neighbor-ip>
            family mcast-vpn
            add-paths
                mvpn-ipv4 send 8 receive
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**2. Group-level configuration (applies to all neighbors in the group):**
```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        family mcast-vpn
        add-paths
            mvpn-ipv4 send 8 receive
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**3. Global BGP configuration (applies to all neighbors):**
```cli
configure router bgp
    add-paths
        mvpn-ipv4 send 8 receive
    exit
exit
```

### Key details:
