To ensure graceful restarts during your maintenance window, configure BGP graceful restart helper functionality and set an appropriate restart-time:

```
configure
    router
        bgp
            graceful-restart
            restart-time 300
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- The `graceful-restart` command activates helper functionality, allowing your router to preserve neighbor adjacencies and maintain forwarding state for restarting peers  
- The `restart-time 300` sets the maximum wait period (300 seconds) for peers to re-establish before withdrawing routes, matching common peer expectations  
- This configuration is applied globally to affect all BGP peers, but can be refined per-group or per-neighbor if required  

These commands ensure your router will:  
1) Retain routes from restarting peers without immediate withdrawal  
2) Maintain existing forwarding paths during peer restarts  
3) Re-establish sessions automatically after peers reboot  
4) Advertise consistent restart capabilities to neighbors  

The configuration uses Nokia's recommended 300-second default restart-time, which provides sufficient time for most peer reboot operations while preventing indefinite route preservation.
